# The Rossler attractor
# The simplest chaotic flow, with a single nonlinear term. The trajectory
# spirals out in the x-y plane and is folded back through z (Rossler, 1976).
x'=-y-z
y'=x+a*y
z'=b+z*(x-c)
par a=0.2,b=0.2,c=5.7
init x=1,y=1,z=0
@ total=300,dt=0.01,meth=rungekutta,maxstor=200000,bound=1000
@ xp=x,yp=y,xlo=-12,xhi=14,ylo=-12,yhi=10
done
